        "\n",
        "# 🧮 Compound Interest\n",
        "\n",
        "The compound interest formula is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A=P\\left(1+\\frac{r}{n}\\right)^{nt}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where:\n",
        "\n",
        "* \\(A\\) = final amount\n",
        "* \\(P\\) = initial principal\n",
        "* \\(r\\) = annual interest rate expressed as a decimal\n",
        "* \\(n\\) = number of compounding periods per year\n",
        "* \\(t\\) = time in years\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, an annual interest rate of **7%** is written as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "r=0.07\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Common compounding frequencies include:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Compounding Frequency | \\(n\\) |\n",
        "| --------------------- | ----: |\n",
        "| Annually              |     1 |\n",
        "| Semiannually          |     2 |\n",
        "| Quarterly             |     4 |\n",
        "| Monthly               |    12 |\n",
        "| Daily                 |   365 |\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# ♾️ Continuous Compounding\n",
        "\n",
        "When interest is compounded continuously, we use the exponential model\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "A=Pe^{rt}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where \\(e\\) is Euler's number:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "e\\approx2.71828\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Continuous compounding represents the mathematical limit of increasingly frequent compounding.\n",
        "\n",
