        "# 5. A More Realistic Investment Scenario\n",
        "\n",
        "Now we will make our example more realistic.\n",
        "\n",
        "Instead of investing $10,000 once and never adding more money, suppose you continue investing every month.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Scenario\n",
        "\n",
        "You start with:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "P=\\$10,000\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "You contribute:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "C=\\$500 \\text{ per month}\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "Your investment earns:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "r=7\\%\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "per year.\n",
        "\n",
        "You continue investing for:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "t=30\\text{ years}\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "This means that over 30 years, you personally contribute:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "\\$10,000 + (30)(12)(\\$500)\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "or:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "\\$190,000\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "The remaining amount comes from **investment growth**.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is where compound growth becomes especially powerful."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UvdIL4UMF71R"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Investment with Monthly Contributions\n",
        "\n",
        "def investment_with_monthly_contributions(\n",
        "    initial_investment,\n",
        "    monthly_contribution,\n",
        "    annual_rate,\n",
        "    years\n",
        "):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Calculate investment growth with monthly contributions.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Interest is compounded monthly.\n",
        "    Contributions are added at the end of each month.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    monthly_rate = annual_rate / 12\n",
        "    total_months = int(years * 12)\n",
        "\n",
        "    balance = initial_investment\n",
        "\n",
        "    records = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for month in range(1, total_months + 1):\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Calculate monthly interest\n",
        "        interest = balance * monthly_rate\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Add interest\n",
        "        balance += interest\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Add monthly contribution\n",
        "        balance += monthly_contribution\n",
        "\n",
        "        records.append({\n",
        "            \"Month\": month,\n",
        "            \"Year\": month / 12,\n",
        "            \"Balance\": balance,\n",
        "            \"Total Contributions\": (\n",
        "                initial_investment +\n",
        "                monthly_contribution * month\n",
        "            ),\n",
        "            \"Interest Earned\": (\n",
        "                balance -\n",
        "                (initial_investment +\n",
        "                 monthly_contribution * month)\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "initial_investment = 0\n",
        "monthly_contribution = 3600\n",
        "annual_rate = 0.07\n",
        "investment_years = 20\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate\n",
        "\n",
        "df_investment = investment_with_monthly_contributions(\n",
        "    initial_investment,\n",
        "    monthly_contribution,\n",
        "    annual_rate,\n",
        "    investment_years\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display final results\n",
        "\n",
        "final_balance = df_investment.iloc[-1][\"Balance\"]\n",
        "total_contributions = df_investment.iloc[-1][\"Total Contributions\"]\n",
        "total_interest = df_investment.iloc[-1][\"Interest Earned\"]\n",
