        "# 8. What Happens If the Interest Rate Changes?\n",
        "\n",
        "The annual return on an investment is extremely important.\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's compare three possible average annual returns:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **5%**\n",
        "- **7%**\n",
        "- **9%**\n",
        "\n",
        "We will keep everything else the same:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Initial investment = \\$10,000\n",
        "- Monthly contribution = $500\n",
        "- Time = 30 years\n",
        "\n",
        "Only the interest rate will change."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aeG-AGQhHNC7"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Compare different annual rates\n",
        "\n",
        "rates = [0.05, 0.07, 0.09]\n",
        "\n",
        "rate_data = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for rate in rates:\n",
        "\n",
        "    df_temp = investment_with_monthly_contributions(\n",
        "        initial_investment,\n",
        "        monthly_contribution,\n",
        "        rate,\n",
        "        investment_years\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    for _, row in df_temp.iterrows():\n",
        "\n",
        "        rate_data.append({\n",
        "            \"Year\": row[\"Year\"],\n",
        "            \"Investment Value\": row[\"Balance\"],\n",
        "            \"Annual Return\": f\"{rate*100:.0f}%\"\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "df_rates = pd.DataFrame(rate_data)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = px.line(\n",
        "    df_rates,\n",
        "    x=\"Year\",\n",
        "    y=\"Investment Value\",\n",
        "    color=\"Annual Return\",\n",
        "    title=\"The Effect of Different Annual Returns\",\n",
        "    labels={\n",
