        "# 🏁 Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "Compound interest is one of the most important mathematical ideas in personal finance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The basic formula is:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "A=P\\left(1+\\frac{r}{n}\\right)^{nt}\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "For continuous compounding:\n",
        "\n",
        "$\n",
        "A=Pe^{rt}\n",
        "$\n",
        "\n",
        "However, real investing often involves **regular contributions**, which makes the investment growth more interesting.\n",
        "\n",
        "Our Python model demonstrates that:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Investing for a longer period can dramatically increase growth.\n",
        "- Higher rates of return can have a large effect over long periods.\n",
        "- Regular contributions can substantially increase the final investment value.\n",
        "- Compound growth becomes increasingly important over time.\n",
        "- Continuous compounding provides a useful mathematical model for understanding the limit of increasingly frequent compounding.\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Big Idea\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Money invested today has more time to grow, and compound growth means that your investment can eventually begin earning money on previously earned money.**\n",
        "\n",
        "Use Python and visualization to explore the mathematics rather than simply memorizing formulas."
